:: Meal Sister Diner Tutor [activity meal] {"position":"1600,2225"}
/*
{
        id: "sister_diner_tutor",
        passage: "Meal Sister Diner Tutor",
        isActive: false,
        mealType: ["breakfast", "lunch", "dinner"],
        isImportant: true,
        dayType: ["weekday", "weekend"],
        cooldown: 0,
        once: true,
        lastSeen: -1,
        present: ["mom", "sister"],
        requirements: [
        ],
        set: [
            () => setup.getMealById("sister_diner_tutor").isActive = false,
        ]
}
   Activated by: "She'd Do Anything For Me" (sister_doAnythingForMe). She decided to wait tables
   at $diner.name and tutor other students, to pay me back and help the family.
*/
$sister.callName has made a flyer.

She lays it next to $mom.callName's plate with both hands, like a waiter presenting the wine list. Bright yellow paper, a cartoon brain wearing sunglasses, and in big bubble letters: CALCULUS, EXPLAINED BY SOMEONE WHO ALMOST FAILED IT. Underneath, smaller: Reasonable rates. No judgment. Snacks negotiable.

/* IMAGE: images/meals/important/sister_diner_tutor.jpg | A bright yellow tutoring flyer with a cartoon brain in sunglasses lying next to a plate. Mom holding it at arm's length to read, Sister watching her reaction proudly. */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Snacks negotiable?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "It's a marketing thing. People respond to snacks." },
{ who: $mom, text: "You're going to tutor? Oh, sweetie, that's wonderful, you always were good at explaining things." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And I'm going to wait tables at $diner.name, a few shifts a week. I already talked to $manager.callName." },
{ text: "$mom.callName puts the flyer down. Her smile stays where it is, but something behind it slips." },
{ who: $mom, text: "The diner? Honey, you don't have to do that. You have your classes, you finally got your grades back up..." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I want to. Everybody in this house is working their butt off except me, and I'm tired of being the one who just takes." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<if setup.questDone("mom_falseSympathy")>>
$mom.callName looks down at her plate, and I know exactly what she's thinking: that $sister.callName is picking up shifts because of what happened at the firm. She doesn't say it, but $sister.callName sees it too and squeezes her arm.
<<else>>
$mom.callName looks down at her plate, and I know exactly what she's thinking: that $sister.callName is picking up shifts because one paycheck doesn't stretch far enough anymore. She doesn't say it, but $sister.callName sees it anyway and squeezes her arm.
<</if>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "It's not a sacrifice, $mom.callName, it's tips. You've seen me be charming. I'm going to make a fortune." },
{ who: $player, text: "The regulars at the counter tip in quarters, just so you know." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Then I'll make a fortune in quarters. And you're going to show me how to carry three plates at once without dying." },
{ who: $player, text: "That's advanced. You start with two." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, I just... thank you, sweetie, both of you. I honestly don't know when you two grew up on me." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

$sister.callName beams. Then she catches my eye across the table, and for a second the beam turns into something softer and more private, a look that says she did this for me as much as for anyone. She folds a second flyer into a paper plane and sails it at my head.

I let it hit me. A month ago she'd have laughed at the idea of working at the diner. Now she's lining up to work there because she wants me to see her do it.

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 2>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 2>>
